# W44-79 follow-on outcome:
#   Discriminator FOUND for 1189261 cells (3 OPEN: e5 d=4, e8 d=3, e9 d=3).
#   Discriminator: `colourfulness >= 80 AND flat_color_block_ratio < 0.01`
#   (zenanalyze Tier 2 features). Per-distance hint A/B confirms -1450 B
#   total savings on 1189261 across d ∈ {3, 4, 5} but +560 B regression
#   at d=6 (caller MUST cap at d <= 5).
#
#   The discriminator does NOT auto-fire in the production hot path
#   (Tier 2 compute too expensive for 1-of-41 EV). Ships as
#   documentation + opt-in pathway via existing
#   `LossyConfig::with_high_d_photo_hint(Some(true))` API.
#
#   See `benchmarks/w44_79_zenanalyze_discriminator_2026-05-19.meta`
#   for full method + per-image features + reproducer.
#
# Reproducer (this refresh):
#   cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' \
#     --example cjxl_parity_ledger -- \
#     --ledger benchmarks/cjxl_parity_ledger_2026-05-19_w44_79.tsv \
#     --update --status OPEN

reproducer (seed): cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' --example cjxl_parity_ledger -- --output <path>
reproducer (update single cell): cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' --example cjxl_parity_ledger -- --ledger <path> --update --image <name> --effort <N> --distance <F>
